			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Update documentation to cross-platform support, Vine integration, and updated toolchain requirements\n\nReflect the multi-platform scope transition from macOS-only to macOS, Windows, and Linux across the architecture overview.\n\nAdd the Vine component to the architectural and build matrix tables, documenting its role as the gRPC protocol layer used between Mountain and Cocoon and between Mountain and Air, with generated stubs consumed by all gRPC-speaking elements.\n\nUpdate the minimum supported Rust version from 1.77+ (Mountain) and 1.75+ (Grove) to a unified 1.95.0+ workspace-wide MSRV. Add Air/Target to the build artifact paths table and include an element-specific build instructions entry for Air. Fix a duplicated \"see see\" phrase in Building.md.\n\nAll documentation now accurately reflects the current component roster, supported platforms, and toolchain baseline.",
			"SHA": "e80d5b624c49dd8ccf4a62111200a95a9ca4a9cf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-30T13:14:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Quote Output package reference in build pipeline diagram\n\nUpdate the Mermaid graph syntax in BuildPipeline.md to wrap the @codeeditorland/output/ node label in quotes. This ensures proper rendering of the package name containing special characters (@ and /) in the dependency visualization.\n\nNo functional changes — purely a documentation syntax correction for correct diagram rendering.",
			"SHA": "7d25daaf03e1aed5779609e2976712ba0c3913f6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-30T13:01:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				4
			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Convert Element submodule links to absolute GitHub URLs\n\nIn Documentation/GitHub/*.md files, replace `blob` with `tree` in absolute GitHub URLs linking to Element submodule documentation. The `blob` keyword fails for submodule-hosted files on GitHub's web interface, while `tree` correctly points to the directory containing the target files.\n\nAffected files: Building.md, README.md, Workflow.md. All Element architecture and deep-dive documentation links now resolve properly on GitHub.com.\n\nSubmodule Element advanced to b80c9381, incorporating dependency updates: Cocoon (protobufjs 8.4.2→8.5.0), Common and Echo (@cloudflare/workers-types bumped), Worker (github-push-action 1.1.0→1.3.0), plus merge commits for Maintain, Mountain, Output, Rest, SideCar, Sky, and Wind.\n\nNo functional changes beyond link resolution and dependency synchronization.",
			"SHA": "a9e02c19f73dca9540f51fd7f58a342c1d429895"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-30T12:54:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				6
			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Convert Element submodule links to absolute GitHub URLs and restore pnpm in build docs\n\nThe Documentation/GitHub/*.md files and README.md contained relative links to Element submodules (e.g., `Element/Mountain/Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md`). These paths resolve correctly on disk but break on GitHub's web interface since Element is a Git submodule with its own remote repository. Convert all Element documentation links to absolute GitHub URLs pointing to each element's repository at the `Current` branch.\n\nAdditionally, restore `pnpm` commands in the build documentation. The `dum` script runner references were removed as the build pipeline now uses `pnpm run` directly. Update Building.md, BuildPipeline.md, Workflow.md, and README.md to reflect this change.\n\nAdd `Element` to the `exclude_path` list in `.lychee.toml` to prevent lychee link checker from flagging the submodule paths as broken (they are now absolute URLs in the docs, but the exclude ensures any remaining raw paths don't trigger false positives).\n\nAll documentation links now resolve correctly on GitHub.com and local file system.",
			"SHA": "4afc6feaa9df3bbb3c9aa6d42db2e7740f830504"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-29T14:23:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Sync Maintain to Node v24 build config\n\nUpdate the Element submodule pointer to 01694669, which advances the Maintain submodule to align the build pipeline with Node.js v24 for the Cocoon extension host sidecar.\n\nThe Build module documentation and test fixtures in Process.rs, Rhai/mod.rs, and mod.rs now reference NODE_VERSION=\"24\" and updated bundle identifiers (24NodeVersion, node.24.debug). This synchronizes the build configuration with the active Node.js versions in the development environment.\n\nNo functional behavior changes beyond version string updates.",
			"SHA": "c3436e1f2cfaccf5a56c09fc54995e9e00e78f52"
		}
	],
